  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — comparing the least probable outcomes (i.e., the worst-case monetary loss) — is present in the verbal report: the individual explicitly compares -3000€ (A) and -6000€ (B) and concludes that -3000€ is more tolerable. The decision reason specifies that it prefers the lottery with the more favorable (less negative) least probable outcome, which matches the individual’s reasoning. The individual’s justification is grounded in the severity of the negative outcome in the low-probability tail, which aligns directly with the rule of the decision reason. Although the individual does not explicitly state the rule or use formal language, the reasoning process clearly reflects the application of the reason. Therefore, the individual used the decision reason to make the decision.",
